## Docker
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
Everything runs in containers. The `dev` service mounts this folder and keeps `target/` and downloaded crates in Docker volumes:

```sh
docker compose run --rm dev cargo fetch             # after cloning
docker compose up dev                               # development loop
docker compose run --rm dev sh scripts/check.sh     # any command
docker compose run --rm --build app --help          # production image
docker compose --profile dev down                   # stop; add --volumes to delete target/ and the crate cache
```
{% else %}
```sh
docker compose build app                          # build the image {{ project.slug }}:latest
docker compose run --rm --build app stats README.md Cargo.toml
docker compose down --rmi all                     # remove the containers and the image
```
{% endif %}
The image contains only the release binary on a minimal base (`gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian13`, non-root user). `docker compose run --rm app <args>` mounts the project folder at `/work`, the working directory, so relative paths work. Compose reads `.env`: `APP_NAME` is passed to the build, `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` names the stack and the image. The tool keeps no state, so there is no data volume.
{% endif %}
